<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yasa</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Yassa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Yasa was the body of law and decrees attributed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genghis-khan">Genghis Khan</a>, governing military discipline, administration and social conduct among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a>. It served as a foundation of Mongol imperial governance. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chagatai-khanate">Chagatai Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a> both upheld the Yasa, and tensions between it and Islamic law arose as their rulers converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>.</p></div>
